lklfuse: passfd=N, an encrypted volume's password from a descriptor

lklfuse reads the password from descriptor N and gives it to the filesystem as pass=HEX in the mount data
(linux-apfs-rw, with linuxfs's encryption patch, unlocks the volume with it), so it is never on a command
line; the buffers that held it are cleared once the mount is done.

